    <sectiondef kind="public-attrib">
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__trigger_1afff4cd79ce8bef5eb16061de39587d90" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>short</type>
        <definition>short threshold</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>threshold</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_trigger::threshold</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Threshold of both triggers units. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Valid values depend on output mode:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__outputdefs_1ga6da4f29b3f6dd4430f78dc2b939e2a2d" kindref="member">NDIGO_OUTPUT_MODE_RAW</ref>: 0 to 1023</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__outputdefs_1ga2590f128181ea4332de3e0e25240758e" kindref="member">NDIGO_OUTPUT_MODE_SIGNED16</ref>: -32768 to +32767</para>
<para>For trigger indices <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1ga965c178fd1642744c3477627eb7de843" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_TDC</ref> to <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1ga1303a942415e4849dd715e9037d33df4" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_BUS3_PE</ref> the threshold is ignored. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_common_interface.h" line="473" column="11" bodyfile="ndigo_common_interface.h" bodystart="473" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__trigger_1a27316febd6206386bbbc8e1310678962" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type><ref refid="ndigo__common__interface_8h_1ac8108da51e15c2c7cd3dadb52ec3efd9" kindref="member">ndigo_bool_t</ref></type>
        <definition>ndigo_bool_t edge</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>edge</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_trigger::edge</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Enable edge trigger functionality. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If true, operate as an edge trigger.</para>
<para>If false, operate as a level trigger.</para>
<para>An edge trigger triggers as soon as its set threshold is crossed by the signal. Thus the roots in reference to the threshold are recorded.</para>
<para>A level trigger triggers as long as the signal is above (or below) the set threshold. Therefore, the trigger gives the sign of the signal in reference to the threshold.</para>
<para>For trigger indices <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1gae88dc2cdeaa20a6c90d8b726c5d5b5a3" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_AUTO</ref> and <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1ga1115f490ea453ff315993927b8424b05" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_ONE</ref> this is ignored.</para>
<para>For trigger indices <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1gab4b66daf69fb38f6aa9ffa47db814876" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_TDC_PE</ref> to <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1ga1303a942415e4849dd715e9037d33df4" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_BUS3_PE</ref> this must be set. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_common_interface.h" line="490" column="18" bodyfile="ndigo_common_interface.h" bodystart="490" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__trigger_1af8473ec25f5ef654d24c79394c4d8312" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type><ref refid="ndigo__common__interface_8h_1ac8108da51e15c2c7cd3dadb52ec3efd9" kindref="member">ndigo_bool_t</ref></type>
        <definition>ndigo_bool_t rising</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>rising</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_trigger::rising</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Configure rising or falling edge trigger functionality. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If true (false)<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="structndigo__trigger_1a27316febd6206386bbbc8e1310678962" kindref="member">ndigo_trigger::edge</ref> is true: Trigger on rising (falling) edges, that is, when the signal level crosses from below to above the value of <ref refid="structndigo__trigger_1afff4cd79ce8bef5eb16061de39587d90" kindref="member">ndigo_trigger::threshold</ref>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="structndigo__trigger_1a27316febd6206386bbbc8e1310678962" kindref="member">ndigo_trigger::edge</ref> is false (level triggering): Trigger parts of the signal that are above (below) the value of <ref refid="structndigo__trigger_1afff4cd79ce8bef5eb16061de39587d90" kindref="member">ndigo_trigger::threshold</ref>.</para>
<para>For trigger indices <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1gae88dc2cdeaa20a6c90d8b726c5d5b5a3" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_AUTO</ref> and <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1ga1115f490ea453ff315993927b8424b05" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_ONE</ref> this is ignored.</para>
<para>For trigger indices <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1gab4b66daf69fb38f6aa9ffa47db814876" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_TDC_PE</ref> to <ref refid="group__triggerdefs_1ga1303a942415e4849dd715e9037d33df4" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_BUS3_PE</ref> this must be set. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_common_interface.h" line="507" column="18" bodyfile="ndigo_common_interface.h" bodystart="507" bodyend="-1"/>
